  "premise_review": [
    "The first theorem retains the whole exact old W : Folder.Arithmetic.CertifiedQuadraticTwistFamily, target Folder.Arithmetic.AllTwistsCertified W.witness and unchanged fully qualified original proof call W. Its provider formula is genuinely universal: ∀ d : W.witness.TwistParam, W.witness.strongBSDCertified d.",
    "The per-parameter strongBSDCertified predicate remains arbitrary supplied proof-family content, with no relation to an actual BSD formula or quadratic-twist construction. The extracted theorem exposes the full already assumed universal certification witness, not a proof of BSD.",
    "The second source theorem genuinely forwards the same full W to its independent chosen isInfiniteFamily proposition. That proposition is not a defined infinitude/cardinality statement, so this complete wrapper stays archive-only with its genuine proof acknowledged.",
    "Neither field of the old certified family is dropped from W in the maintained theorem. The original legacy import and all qualified proof/type bindings remain unchanged; no new260 provider or root-path alias is substituted.",
    "The exact root BSDTwistWitness capture was fully read independently as260 and has matching declared Folder.Arithmetic names but its root physical hint is not Arithmetic/BSDTwistWitness. It is contextual evidence only, not activated as the canonical imported module."
  ],
